 "name": "mols39-lemmaU-certificate-wave-v3",
 "nc9": {
  "derivation": "The only change is D[1][0]: 0 -> 1 (row 1, column 0). For the pair (0,1), f(c) = D[0][c] - D[1][c] (mod 39) was a bijection of the 39 columns onto Z_39 (the anchor is a DM, checked by the accepted checker in CHK-nc0 and CHK-anchor). At c = 0, f(0) changes from 0 - 0 = 0 to 0 - 1 = 38. The value 38 was already taken at exactly one other column, so 38 now occurs twice and 0 no longer occurs: f is not a bijection. The checker tests the pairs in lexicographic order, (0,1) first, after the hash, shape and q/U/J tests, which the mutated file passes (same shape, and the certificate names its hash). So its first failure is exactly 'check 1: D is not a difference matrix (rows 0, 1)', the preregistered reason for CHK-nc9_anchor_mutation.",
  "mutated_row1_line": "1 16 23 4 35 0 0 4 35 23 16 0 0 8 31 13 26 0 0 16 23 5 34 0 0 7 32 12 27 0 0 38 1 11 28 0 0 15 24",
  "original_row1_line": "0 16 23 4 35 0 0 4 35 23 16 0 0 8 31 13 26 0 0 16 23 5 34 0 0 7 32 12 27 0 0 38 1 11 28 0 0 15 24",
